## BEV Scorer Phase-1 Training

- Launcher: `scripts/training/run_drivor_bev_phase1.sh`
- Config entry: `navsim/planning/script/config/training/default_training.yaml` (loaded via `run_training_full.py` Hydra `CONFIG_NAME`).
- Intent: load pretrained DrivoR checkpoint, freeze the original network, train only `bev_tokenizer.*`, `scorer_attention.layers.*.cross_attn_bev*`, and `*_lora.*`.
- BEV tensors are `decoder_neck` features, shape `(256, 128, 128)`.
- `area_pred=false` and `agent_pred=false` → `pred_ce_loss`, `pred_l1_loss`, `pred_area_loss` are always 0; this is expected.
- LR uses sqrt scaling: `lr = base_lr * sqrt(global_batch / base_batch_size)` — no manual LR adjustment needed when changing batch.
- Typical speed: 2GPU/16batch/8worker ≈ 5.8hr/epoch (with dataset cache); 85109 train samples, 18179 val samples.
- BEV scorer structure config lives in `navsim/planning/script/config/common/agent/drivoR.yaml`:
  - `scorer_bev: {lora_rank=8, lora_dropout, add_new_cross_attn=true, init_gate=0.0}`
  - `bev_tokenizer: {patch_size=8, num_tokens=64, use_self_attn_block=false}`
- Both the training and eval scripts expose env vars `SCORER_BEV_LORA_RANK` and `SCORER_BEV_INIT_GATE` (defaults 16 / 0.1) to override the yaml.
- `cross_attn_bev_ls.gamma` (LayerScale, init = `init_gate`) gates how much BEV affects each scorer block; inspect it to verify BEV is actually used. With `init_gate=0.0` it trains to only |gamma|≈0.01–0.02 (BEV ≈ 1–2% of the residual), explaining marginal gains.

## BEV Decoder Phase-1 Training (trajectory generator)

- Canonical architecture and maintenance specification:
  `docs/architecture/bev-trajectory-decoder.md`. Read it before changing the
  decoder, tokenizer, checkpoint whitelist, or decoder-BEV evaluation config.

- Same launcher `scripts/training/run_drivor_bev_phase1.sh`; defaults now target **decoder-only** BEV:
  - `USE_BEV_IN_SCORER=false`, `USE_BEV_IN_DECODER=true`
  - `DECODER_BEV_INIT_GATE=0.0`, `DECODER_BEV_LORA_RANK=16`
- Architecture: `BevAwareTrajectoryDecoder` in `navsim/agents/drivoR/layers/bev_decoder_blocks.py`
  - Per block (sequential): `q += q_cam + gate * q_bev` via separate camera cross-attn then BEV cross-attn sublayer.
  - Optional side-LoRA on frozen self-attn, camera cross-attn, and MLP when `decoder_bev.lora_rank > 0`.
- Trainable (phase-1): `bev_tokenizer.*`, `trajectory_decoder.layers.*.cross_attn_bev*`, `trajectory_decoder.layers.*.*_lora.*`.
- Frozen: entire backbone + original decoder weights + scorer (when `use_bev_in_scorer=false`).
- Config keys in `drivoR.yaml`: `use_bev_in_scorer`, `use_bev_in_decoder`, `decoder_bev: {init_gate, lora_rank, lora_dropout}`.
- Parity test: `scripts/training/test_drivor_bev_decoder_parity.py` (gate=0 lora=0 → bit-identical to `TransformerDecoder`).
- Reference run: `exp/ke/Jun12-golduck-4gpu-lora16-bev-decoder/06.12_01.12/checkpoints/last.ckpt` (30 epochs, 4×A100).

## BEV Residual Proposal Refiner

- Branch: `dev-bev-residual-proposal-refiner`.
- Architecture registry: `docs/architecture/bev-injection-alternatives.md`.
- Injection is post-decoder and pre-scorer; original DrivoR remains frozen.
- Trainable: `bev_tokenizer.*` and `bev_residual_proposal_refiner.*`.
- Default: one global path-query BEV cross-attention block and scalar
  `alpha=0.0`, followed by an `(8, 3)` delta head for every proposal.
- Launcher: `scripts/training/run_drivor_bev_residual_proposal_refiner.sh`.

## Dataset Caching

- Script: `scripts/training/run_dataset_caching.sh` → calls `navsim/planning/script/run_dataset_caching.py`.
- **Critical**: Cache must be generated with the **exact same agent config** as training. Key params that change sample schema:
  - `agent.config.long_trajectory_additional_poses=2` (adds `trajectory_long` key)
  - `agent.config.use_bev_feature=true` / `bev_feature_type` / `bev_channels` / `bev_features_root` / `bev_data_split`
- Mismatch causes `KeyError` at DataLoader collation (e.g. `KeyError: 'trajectory_long'`).
- Use `worker=sequential` for stability; Ray workers tend to crash during caching.
- Cache loading is fast (~seconds for 85k samples) vs SceneLoader initialization (30+ hours).

## Multi-GPU / DDP

- Strategy: `ddp_find_unused_parameters_true` (frozen params require it).
- `run_training_full.py` uses `LocalMetadataDDPStrategy` to avoid NCCL object broadcasts for identical local metadata.
- W&B logger is instantiated **only on rank 0**; other ranks get `logger=False` and `LearningRateMonitor` is filtered out.
- Ray scorer is disabled during multi-GPU training (`use_ray_score=false` when `num_gpus > 1`).

## Memory & Stability

- **CPU RAM is the kill-zone**: `BATCH_SIZE × NUM_GPUS × NUM_WORKERS × PREFETCH_FACTOR × ~16 MB/sample` must fit in ~125 GB.
- Safe starting point: `BATCH_SIZE=8 NUM_WORKERS=2 PREFETCH_FACTOR=1`; scale up batch while reducing workers.
- For larger effective batch without more RAM: use `trainer.params.accumulate_grad_batches`.
- Process `Killed` (SIGKILL) with no Python traceback = system OOM; check `launcher.log` for exit code and timing.
- `pin_memory=true` (from yaml default) increases pinned RAM footprint; disable if RAM-constrained.

## Logging & Metrics (PL + WandB)

- `launcher.log` (in experiment output dir) captures full stdout/stderr, exit code, and timestamps.
- `run_training_full.log` is Hydra's main process log; `train_ddp_process_*.log` for sub-ranks.
- W&B local data: `exp/ke/<experiment>/<uid>/wandb/run-*/`; if process was killed, run `wandb sync <dir>` to upload.
- **PL metric naming rules**:
  - `on_step=True, on_epoch=True` → PL auto-appends `_step` and `_epoch` suffixes (two metrics).
  - `on_step=True, on_epoch=False` → metric name stays as-is, logged every step.
  - `on_step=False, on_epoch=True` → metric name stays as-is, logged once per epoch.
- Current config:
  - `train/loss`: `on_step=True, on_epoch=True` → WandB shows `train/loss_step` and `train/loss_epoch`.
  - Other train losses (trajectory_loss, etc.): `on_step=True, on_epoch=False` → WandB shows original name, logged every step.
  - `val/score`: `on_step=True, on_epoch=True` → produces `val/score_epoch` for `ModelCheckpoint(monitor='val/score_epoch')`.
  - Other val metrics: `on_step=False, on_epoch=True` → original name, logged once per epoch.

## NAVSIM Evaluation (v1 PDMS / v2 EPDMS)

- **v1 (navtest, open-loop PDMS)**: single-frame planning score. Env `drivoR-share`. Set `NAVSIM_DEVKIT_ROOT=DrivoR`.
  - Scorer-BEV: `scripts/evaluation/run_drivor_bev_evaluation.sh`
  - Decoder-BEV: `scripts/evaluation/run_drivor_bev_decoder_evaluation.sh` (`use_bev_in_decoder=true`, `decoder_bev.lora_rank=16`)
  - Proposal-world: `scripts/evaluation/run_drivor_proposal_world_evaluation.sh` (`use_proposal_world_refiner=true`, all other BEV injection flags false)
- **v2 (navhard_two_stage, closed-loop EPDMS)**: two-stage reactive eval; one run yields **stage_one**, **stage_two**, and **combined** scores. Env `drivoR-share`. Set `NAVSIM_DEVKIT_ROOT=navsim`.
  - Decoder-BEV: `navsim/scripts/evaluation/run_drivoR_pdm_score_v2_decoder_bev.sh`; skill `drivor-navsim-v2-eval`.
  - Scorer-BEV: `navsim/scripts/evaluation/run_drivoR_pdm_score_v2.sh`
- v2 requires decoder-BEV code synced into `navsim/navsim/agents/drivoR/` (`bev_decoder_blocks.py`, `drivor_model.py`, `drivoR.yaml`, agent whitelist).
- **PYTHONPATH**: v2 scripts set `PYTHONPATH=$NAVSIM_DEVKIT_ROOT:...` because `drivoR-share` egg-link registers DrivoR's older `navsim` package (lacks `scene_aggregator`).
- **Python 3.9 required for v2**: `drivoR-share` is now py3.9; older py3.8 breaks `nuplan-devkit` `StateIndex.STATE_SE2` → `IndexError` in scoring.
- Eval Hydra: `agent.loss=null`, `num_epochs=1`, `batch_size=1`, `worker=sequential`; quote checkpoint paths containing `=`.
- v2 metric weights: `noc=10 dac=13 ddc=6 ttc=14 ep=15 comfort=2`.
- **Long v2 runs (~2.5 h, 5912 scenarios)**: use `setsid nohup bash ... > exp/v2_full_*.log 2>&1 &` — Cursor background terminals can kill child processes mid-run.
- **`max_scenes` smoke**: inference may pass but aggregation fails (`Missing token in score_df`) because two-frame comfort needs full token chain; use full split for official score.

